1. WheelLog (Wheellog.Android): protocol test data
--------------------------------------------------

   Project:  WheelLog for Android
   Source:   https://github.com/Wheellog/Wheellog.Android
   License:  GNU General Public License, version 3 (GPL-3.0)

Some of the protocol test vectors in RideFlux's unit tests were taken from
WheelLog's repository, and are credited here. They are used by the tests only:
they are not part of the phone app, the glasses HUD app, or any APK or AAB built
from this repository. To the extent this material is protected by copyright,
WheelLog's license applies to it.

File paths below are relative to
data/protocol/src/test/kotlin/com/rideflux/protocol/ in this repository; the
paths after "Taken from" are relative to app/src/ in the WheelLog repository.

   familyg/BegodeDecoderTest.kt
       The two sample frames "A" (live telemetry) and "B" (settings and
       odometer).
       Taken from: main/java/com/cooper/wheellog/utils/GotwayAdapter.java, the
       comment titled "Gotway/Begode reverse-engineered protocol".

   familyg/BegodeBatteryPackTest.kt
       Sample frame "A" from the same comment, with its voltage field changed.

   familyv/VeteranRealFrameTest.kt
   familyv/VeteranDecoderTest.kt
       Real Veteran frames: three in the first file; the second file uses one
       of the same three.
       Taken from: test/java/com/cooper/wheellog/utils/VeteranAdapterTest.kt

   familyi1/InmotionI1RealFrames.kt
       Five InMotion V5F frames, shared by InmotionI1EscapedCheckTest.kt,
       InmotionI1SignednessTest.kt and InmotionI1SplitEscapeTest.kt.
       Taken from: test/resources/RAW_inmotion_V5F.csv

Beyond these test vectors, RideFlux's decoders are its own Kotlin code, but they
were written with reference to open-source projects, WheelLog among them. The
phone app's dashboard (top toolbar and half-disc speedometer) is styled after
WheelLog's.


